The spec is unusually rigorous — the reasoning, the judgment_call flagging, the non_goals are all better than most specs I gate. But it verified against `~/Projects/michi`'s **working tree** while pinning a **tag 68 commits behind it**, and the intervening restructure moved every file it cites and added three of the APIs it depends on. Everything the spec says about michi is true of HEAD; the dependency it actually specifies won't compile. That single mismatch invalidates AC-011, AC-014, AC-015, and the citations in AC-001/AC-003/linked_research at once.

Blockers 5, 6, and 7 are independent of the pin and need fixing regardless. Note that AC-001 and AC-013 survived scrutiny fully intact at both versions, and AC-002/004/005/006/007/008/009/012/016 are all implementable exactly as written once the pin is corrected.

