      "id": "AC-004",
      "criterion": "BindingKind's camelCase JSON forms are exactly: Named->\"named\", Default->\"default\", Namespace->\"namespace\", Glob->\"glob\", NamespaceWide->\"namespaceWide\". For NamespaceWide, serde's variant-level camelCase rule (lowercase only the leading character, per SPEC-003 AC-002's established finding) already produces the fully correct camelCase spelling here, because Rust's PascalCase variant-naming convention marks NamespaceWide's internal word boundary via capitalization (Namespace + Wide) rather than via an underscore -- unlike a snake_case struct field name, no further restructuring is needed to reach \"namespaceWide\".",
